WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.790
If superheroes are great on their own, then
mashing up two different superheroes to create

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.600
a weird new character should be even better,
right?

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.420
Well, that’s not always the case.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.210
The long history of Marvel Comics creating
“mashup” characters has produced some

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.900
classics, but we’ve seen plenty of bad ones,
too.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.100
Best: Weapon H

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.590
The Incredible Hulk and Wolverine circled
each other for years in a long, bloody rivalry,

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:31.590
with Wolverine’s unbreakable bones and adamantium
claws matched up against Hulk’s indomitable

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.010
strength, with both sporting healing factors
that render them nearly impossible to kill.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:39.440
Put all of that together and you get Marvel's
ultimate weapon.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.270
Weapon H was the product of the infamous Weapon
X program, responsible for the creation of

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.460
Wolverine and Deadpool, among others.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.900
This time, they stole DNA from the Totally
Awesome Hulk and Old Man Logan, to create

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.420
an utterly unbeatable weapon, and they succeeded.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:01.140
The idea of a "Hulkverine" might sound like
an unimaginative marketing ploy, but Weapon

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.280
H was at the center of a compelling, action-packed,
and suspenseful story.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.440
Unsurprisingly for anyone who read “Weapons
of Mutant Destruction,” Marvel greenlit

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.600
the ongoing monthly Weapon H not long after
the event's conclusion.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.040
Worst: Captain Punisher

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:21.920
Civil War changed the Marvel Universe drastically,
and one of its darkest moments brought the

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.810
assassination of Captain America.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.900
In the aftermath, the Punisher decided he
would take the job.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.740
In Punisher War Journal #7, while investigating
a violent white supremacist group, Frank Castle

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:39.800
donned a new red, white, blue, and black costume
that combined Cap’s look and his own signature

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:40.300
skulls.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.200
Castle's apparent admiration for the late
Captain didn't inspire Punisher to change

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.780
his methods, though, and he wasn’t nearly
as successful in the role as Steve Rogers.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:54.720
Captain Punisher only lasted four issues,
and never felt like it was meant to last much

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.220
longer.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.700
If his ill-fated adventure hadn’t been enough
of a sign that he should hang up the stars

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.340
and stripes, a confrontation with Bucky Barnes,
who actually would become the new Captain

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.400
America, was enough to make Frank decide that
being a Star-Spangled Avenger just wasn’t

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:09.900
for him.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.740
Best: Storm, Goddess of Thunder

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.000
During a time when Storm of the X-Men had
lost all of her weather-controlling powers,

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:23.200
she found herself in Asgard, where Loki tempted
her with a gift of what seemed to be the power

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:23.700
of Thor.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:29.540
When the New Mutants and X-Men arrived, Loki's
magic clouded her senses, making her see them

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.560
all as villains.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:36.100
At the story's climax, Loki unveiled a hammer
called Stormcaster that he'd crafted for Storm,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.120
which allowed her to nearly kill Wolverine
with its magic, and even give the death goddess

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.940
Hela a run for her money.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.640
Eventually, Storm was able to see through
the illusions, relinquishing the thundering

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.800
power rather than keeping it and becoming
Loki’s pawn.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.080
That wasn’t the last appearance of this
version of Storm, though.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:59.169
Recent issues revealed a glimpse of Storm
in the future, once again becoming an Asgardian

00:02:59.169 --> 00:03:00.160
goddess of thunder.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.460
Worst: WendiHulk

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.020
When Jeph Loeb and Ed McGuinness took over
the Hulk's title in 2008, they kicked things

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:12.840
off by giving the world one popular alternate
version of the green goliath: the Red Hulk.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.299
Eight issues later, readers got a brief look
at a version of Bruce Banner who was nowhere

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.560
near as compelling: the WendiHulk.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:26.040
Finding himself in a tussle with not just
one Wendigo, but a whole army of them, the

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:31.799
green Hulk was transformed into a giant, green,
clawed, fanged, and furry monster who did

00:03:31.799 --> 00:03:36.290
little more than look gnarly and yell "WENDIHULK!"
a lot.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:41.080
Brother Voodoo appeared out of nowhere (literally),
cured him, and that was that.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.180
Best: Spider-Gwen

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.480
Gwen Stacy's tragic demise might be the most
famous and long-standing deaths in superhero

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.120
comic history, but on another Earth, Gwen
never died.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:58.230
Instead, it was her, not Peter Parker, who
received a fateful bite from a radioactive

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.200
spider and used the resulting powers to fight
crime as Spider-Woman.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:07.940
Spider-Gwen was introduced in Edge of Spider-Verse,
and she was an immediate hit with readers,

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.620
emerging from the event with her own monthly
title.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:16.140
She's since become a fixture at Marvel, appearing
in cartoons and video games, and she's one

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.730
of the characters set to appear in the upcoming
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse movie.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.820
She’s more than just a cool spinoff with
a killer costume design, though.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.120
The death of the main continuity’s Gwen
Stacy in 1973 is generally seen as one of

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:35.460
the more important moments in superhero comics,
but it also made her one of the earliest female

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:40.080
comic book characters to be killed just to
further a male protagonist's plotline.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:45.100
That Spider-Gwen became a breakout character
shows that superheroes are moving in the right

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.360
direction, without removing the tragedy of
the original story.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.580
Worst: The Teenage Hulk

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.750
In the late '70s, Marvel started publishing
What If, giving readers alternate versions

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:57.740
of classic stories.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:02.840
In its 12th issue, we got the story of what
would happen if Bruce Banner didn't get caught

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.790
in a gamma blast while trying to save a teenager
named Rick Jones.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:10.460
Instead, it was Rick himself who got belted
with gamma rays.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.980
The teenage Hulk of What If #12 was hilarious.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:18.780
Like the original Rick Jones, he spouted dialogue
that definitely feels like it was written

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:24.000
by adults who were trying, and failing, to
reproduce the cool slang of the youth.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:29.480
He called Bruce Banner a square, grunted that
the soldiers hunting him down armed with “shivs”

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:34.720
and “heaters” were “uncool," before
deciding to "split" or "cut out."

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.740
When he agreed to join the Avengers, it was
because, "Hulk digs it!"

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:44.080
When he battled Annihilus in the Negative
Zone, he urged the villain, "Don't jive Hulk!"

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.560
The Rick Jones of the regular Marvel Universe
would actually become the Hulk for a short

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.760
period, but never enjoyed this kind of wonderful
dialogue.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.820
Best: Franken-Castle

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.700
There are a lot of Marvel mashups that were
created in the pages of What If or other weird

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:05.300
timelines, so if you saw the words “Franken-Castle”
and thought it was the product of an alternate

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.830
reality, that’s understandable.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.440
The truth, however, is that this one is 100%
canon.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:16.860
After helping to thwart an alien invasion
by shooting the Skrull Queen, Norman Osborn,

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:22.160
better known to Spider-Man fans as the Green
Goblin, was named the head of Homeland Security.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:27.180
This did not sit well with the Punisher, but
his attempt at assassinating Osborn didn’t

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.060
go as planned.

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:33.620
Instead, on Osborn’s orders the Punisher
himself was killed by Wolverine’s son Daken,

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:37.150
who literally chopped Frank into pieces and
threw him in the sewer.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.020
The thing is, Frank didn’t die.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:43.870
Instead, the Punisher awoke to find himself
pieced together by the vampire Morbius, who

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.220
recruited him to protect an underground city
of monsters.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:52.750
With his corpse stitched up and reanimated
by a mystical artifact called the Bloodstone,

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:58.050
he was rechristened as “Franken-Castle,”
and stayed that way for an entire year.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:03.639
Eventually, the Bloodstone’s magic regenerated
his human body, but it remains the Punisher’s

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:08.950
most bizarre adventure ever, even weirder
than the time he was a ghost who killed angels

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.320
with magic guns.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.100
Worst: Piecemeal

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:17.960
Superheroes aren't the only ones who get mashed
up; but in the case of Piecemeal, maybe it

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:19.640
would've been better if they were.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:25.740
Shortly after its explosive 400th issue, Incredible
Hulk teased its readers by revealing small

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.940
glimpses of a new and seemingly unstoppable
villain.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:35.280
Finally, Piecemeal struck in Incredible Hulk
#407, and didn’t quite live up to the hype.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:40.540
Piecemeal had the power to absorb and reproduce
the abilities and appearance of super-powered

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:45.840
people, and in his first appearance, he looked
to have the cybernetic arms of Silvermane,

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:51.320
the clawed hands of Sabretooth, the face of
the Red Skull, the chest piece of Attuma,

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.840
and the facial hair of…

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.180
Abraham Lincoln maybe?

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:01.020
Even with the mighty beard of our 16th President,
Piecemeal failed to be much of a threat to

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:01.520
the Hulk.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:07.060
After months of buildup, he was speared through
the torso and tossed into Loch Ness, which

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.560
was the last anyone ever saw of him.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.540
Best: Cosmic Ghost Rider

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:19.060
Most mashup characters stop after combining
two heroes, but Thanos #13 introduced the

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:24.389
world to Cosmic Ghost Rider, a full-on combo
meal of the Punisher, Ghost Rider, Silver

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:26.340
Surfer, and maybe even Deadpool.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:32.860
After the last of Earth's superheroes fell
at Thanos' hands, a dying Frank Castle, aka

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.860
The Punisher, made a deal with the demonic
Mephisto.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:41.029
Marvel’s devilish villain cursed him with
the power of the Ghost Rider, a demonic force

00:08:41.029 --> 00:08:43.200
tasked with punishing the guilty.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.160
With no one left on Earth, though, Castle
went insane, and when Galactus journeyed to

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:53.269
Earth, looking for allies against Thanos,
this new Ghost Rider offered to become his

00:08:53.269 --> 00:08:56.900
new herald, gaining the cosmic power of the
Silver Surfer.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:02.860
Of course, Thanos eventually killed Galactus,
but he and Cosmic Ghost Rider found themselves

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:07.629
unable to kill each other, and eventually
teamed up as Marvel’s oddest possible version

00:09:07.629 --> 00:09:08.880
of the odd couple.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.680
Worst: D-Man

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.740
D-Man, aka Demolition Man, isn't really a
Marvel mash-up.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.259
He’s just a guy with a really bad costume.

00:09:19.259 --> 00:09:24.350
Dennis Dunphy was introduced as a wrestler
who was part of the Unlimited Class Wrestling

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:29.019
Federation, a wrestling organization for people
with superhuman physical attributes.

00:09:29.019 --> 00:09:34.870
He was a star in the ring with the enhanced
strength he received by using an addictive

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.420
drug peddled by the Power Broker.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:44.009
Eventually, Dunphy left the UCWF to help Captain
America take the Broker down, and designed

00:09:44.009 --> 00:09:48.620
the costume he's most known for: a mask made
to look like Wolverine's, and the rest of

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:52.240
the outfit based on Daredevil's original red-and-yellow
suit.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:57.920
D-Man has since become little more than a
joke in Marvel Comics, a character so minor

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:03.699
and so unloved he regularly goes through traumatic
changes, including dying, only to show up

00:10:03.699 --> 00:10:07.220
the next time without anyone explaining how
he got better.

